Keep a second stack with the minimum at each level, so getMin is O(1).
```python
class MinStack:
    def __init__(self): self.s, self.m = [], []
    def push(self, x):
        self.s.append(x); self.m.append(min(x, self.m[-1]) if self.m else x)
    def pop(self): self.s.pop(); self.m.pop()
    def top(self): return self.s[-1]
    def getMin(self): return self.m[-1]
```

Monotonic decreasing stack of indices; when a warmer day arrives, resolve the colder days waiting on the stack. O(n).
```python
def daily(t):
    res, st = [0] * len(t), []
    for i, x in enumerate(t):
        while st and t[st[-1]] < x:
            j = st.pop(); res[j] = i - j
        st.append(i)
    return res
```

