O(n log n): keep `tails[i]` = smallest possible tail of an increasing subsequence of length i + 1.
```python
from bisect import bisect_left
def lis(nums):
    tails = []
    for x in nums:
        i = bisect_left(tails, x)
        if i == len(tails): tails.append(x)
        else: tails[i] = x
    return len(tails)
```
The simpler O(n^2) DP: dp[i] = 1 + max(dp[j] for j < i if nums[j] < nums[i]).

